=== references/D002-disposition.md ===
# D002 disposition — local source observation completed

## Result

**R009 succeeds:** under the approved trusted-development model, [the actual unmodified seam](../runs/R009/README.md) emitted `user-agent: claude-cli/2.1.198 (external, sdk-cli)` and `x-anthropic-billing-header: cc_version=2.1.198.bb7; cc_entrypoint=sdk-cli; cch=00000;` in both repetitions. All 12 protections per repetition passed, with matching outputs and exit 0. The source mechanism is now observed for the pinned fixture/revision; production cause, runtime attribution and identity-only repair sufficiency remain unconfirmed. Exact output and parent evaluation are retained in R009; [independent result review](../checks/D002-result-review-001.json) passed with no material findings, independently recomputing the classification and protection results. The authorized local observation slice is complete. Owner source remains unchanged.

**Subsequent operator decision:** Brent reports routine builds of this binary on the same host and approved dropping the custom sandbox in favor of the trusted local-development model. [D002-r5](D002-r5/contract.md) preserves the source/test and practical monitor; focused call-path/launcher review passed before the successful R009 execution. The proposed sandbox diagnosis below is superseded, not a prerequisite for r5. Local checkpoint commits are authorized; pushes remain operator-controlled. Earlier frozen sandbox contracts still describe their own attempts, not the newly approved boundary.

**Earlier r4 result:** that retry passed Cargo startup and began dependency compilation, but failed before the proxy seam test. R008 remains a build-environment finding; it is superseded by R009 for the local mutation observation, not rewritten.

## Earlier attempt — R008 dependency build failure

[Independent review 004](../checks/D002-review-004.json) passed the exact single-file exception. The parent ran the authorized retry once; [R008](../runs/R008/README.md) retains the command, complete outputs and follow-up checks. Cargo exited 101: `rustix` failed at subprocess setup/spawn with `PermissionDenied`, and `aws-lc-sys` C checks could not find standard headers. Dependency compilation and build-script execution occurred; the proxy test did not. The precise denied operation and reason for failed SDK/header discovery remain unverified. No further permission expansion or retry occurred.

The monitor recorded no observed detachments, errors or known survivors. Parent verification checked all 34 bindings and all 219 known identities across qualification/build, with no known live survivors; owner checkout remains clean. The accepted polling blind spot remains. Next proposed work is narrow synthetic toolchain diagnosis under the existing policy, not another speculative exception. Preserve the partially populated target and consumed r4 marker.

## Earlier attempt — R007 Cargo startup denied

Brent accepted the practical monitoring risk, and [independent review 003](../checks/D002-review-003.json) passed the exact [D002-r3 contract](D002-r3/contract.md). The parent then invoked its one-attempt launcher. [R007](../runs/R007/r3-process-result.json) retains the real command, timestamps, input/output hashes and monitoring reports; [stderr](../runs/R007/r3-stderr.txt) records LibreSSL initialization failing to open `/private/etc/ssl/openssl.cnf` under the unchanged sandbox. Cargo exited 1 before compilation. Same-profile qualification passed; no escapes, monitoring errors or known live survivors were reported, and post-input verification passed.

A bounded [Cargo version-only startup check](../checks/D002-cargo-startup-001.json) with `OPENSSL_CONF=/dev/null` also failed on the same file. No system configuration file was read, no read grant was added, and the primary attempt was not retried. There are zero probe observations; H001/H002 remain untested by execution. The process-monitoring risk is accepted and is **not** the current blocker.

**Exception authorized:** Brent selected “Allow the single-file read-only exception and retry.” [D002-r4](D002-r4/contract.md) adds only the exact config-file read grant, binds the inspected configuration bytes and retains new attempt/output names. Its qualification permits that read while denying config writes and unrelated system-file reads; Cargo version-only startup succeeded. Independent delta review passed and the retry is retained as R008 above. Do not reuse the consumed r3 attempt marker, modify frozen files, or broadly grant access to `/private/etc`. Network, credentials, owner-source edits, downloads and deployment remain excluded.

The clean local owner checkout is pinned at `db3ec743132eb51aa28c210e8bbdd93c68198e55`. The selected seam is the actual `AnthropicOAuthProvider::prepare_request`, called before forwarding. Its source visibly inserts the old user-agent and billing constants and `x-app: cli`; static inspection does not upgrade these to observed output or deployed behavior. H001 remains the leading historical hypothesis; H002, runtime attribution and vendor acceptance remain unresolved.

## Retained evidence and lineage

- [D002 revision 1](D002/contract.md), [frozen manifest](D002/input-manifest.json) and exact source archive preserve initial preparation. [Independent review 001](../checks/D002-review-001.json) rejected the overbroad allow-default filesystem profile before owner execution.
- [D002-r2](D002-r2/contract.md), [manifest](D002-r2/input-manifest.json), and [qualification log](D002-r2/qualification-log.json) retain the separate fix context's regression-first checks. Original D002 bytes remain unchanged.
